An **angle of elevation** is measured up from the horizontal to the line of sight; an **angle of depression** is measured down from it.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (P) at (0,0);
\coordinate (O) at (4.2,0);
\coordinate (T) at (4.2,2.8);
\coordinate (H) at (1.0,2.8);
\draw (-1.0,0) -- (5.4,0);
\draw (P) -- (T);
\draw (O) -- (T);
\draw[dashed] (T) -- (H);
\coordinate (op) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(P)$);
\coordinate (ot) at ($(O)!0.3cm!(T)$);
\draw (op) -- ($(op)+(ot)-(O)$) -- (ot);
\pic[draw, "$\alpha$", angle radius=1.0cm, angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=O--P--T};
\pic[draw, "$\beta$", angle radius=1.0cm, angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=H--T--P};
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[below right] at (O) {$O$};
\node[above right] at (T) {$T$};
\node[font=\small, below] at (1.4,-0.15) {angle of elevation $\alpha$};
\node[font=\small, above] at (2.2,2.95) {angle of depression $\beta$};
\node[font=\small, left] at (H) {horizontal};
\node[font=\small, right] at (5.4,0) {ground};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
A rectangular box $ABCD-EFGH$ has base dimensions $AB = 8\text{ cm}$, $BC = 6\text{ cm}$, and vertical height $CG = 5\text{ cm}$.
Calculate the angle of inclination $\theta$ that the space diagonal $AG$ makes with the base plane $ABCD$, correct to the nearest degree.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.0,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.0,1.2);
\coordinate (D) at (2.0,1.2);
\coordinate (E) at (0,2.5);
\coordinate (F) at (4.0,2.5);
\coordinate (G) at (6.0,3.7);
\coordinate (H) at (2.0,3.7);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, below right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\draw (C) -- (G) node[midway, right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (F) -- (G) -- (H) -- (E) -- (F);
\draw (E) -- (A);
\draw[dashed] (A) -- (D) -- (C);
\draw[dashed] (D) -- (H);
\draw[dashed] (A) -- (C);
\draw (A) -- (G);
\coordinate (ca) at ($(C)!0.32cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (cg) at ($(C)!0.32cm!(G)$);
\draw (ca) -- ($(ca)+(cg)-(C)$) -- (cg);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=C--A--G};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above left] at (D) {$D$};
\node[above left] at (E) {$E$};
\node[above right] at (F) {$F$};
\node[above right] at (G) {$G$};
\node[above left] at (H) {$H$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A right pyramid has a square base $ABCD$ of side length $14\text{ cm}$ and vertical height $OT = 10\text{ cm}$, where $O$ is the centre of the base.
If $M$ is the midpoint of base side $AB$, calculate the angle of inclination $\theta$ of the triangular face $TAB$ to the base, correct to 1 decimal place.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.4,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.0,1.4);
\coordinate (D) at (1.6,1.4);
\coordinate (O) at (3.0,0.7);
\coordinate (M) at (2.2,0);
\coordinate (T) at (3.0,3.8);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[pos=0.78, below] {$14\text{ cm}$};
\draw (B) -- (C);
\draw[dashed] (C) -- (D) -- (A);
\draw (T) -- (A);
\draw (T) -- (B);
\draw (T) -- (C);
\draw[dashed] (T) -- (D);
\draw[dashed] (T) -- (O) node[midway, right] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\draw[dashed] (O) -- (M);
\draw (T) -- (M);
\coordinate (om) at ($(O)!0.32cm!(M)$);
\coordinate (ot) at ($(O)!0.32cm!(T)$);
\draw (om) -- ($(om)+(ot)-(O)$) -- (ot);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=O--M--T};
