A surveyor at point $A$ on flat ground observes a vertical tower due north with an angle of elevation of $20^{\circ}$.
After walking $50\text{ m}$ due east to point $B$, the angle of elevation of the top of the tower from $B$ is $15^{\circ}$.
If $F$ is the foot of the tower, calculate the height $h$ of the tower, correct to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.0,0);
\coordinate (F) at (1.0,2.0);
\coordinate (T) at (1.0,4.4);
\draw[thick] (F) -- (T);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, below] {$50\text{ m}$};
\draw[dashed] (F) -- (A);
\draw[dashed] (F) -- (B);
\draw (A) -- (T);
\draw (B) -- (T);
\coordinate (af) at ($(A)!0.32cm!(F)$);
\coordinate (ab) at ($(A)!0.32cm!(B)$);
\draw (af) -- ($(af)+(ab)-(A)$) -- (ab);
\coordinate (fa) at ($(F)!0.32cm!(A)$);
\coordinate (ft) at ($(F)!0.32cm!(T)$);
\draw (fa) -- ($(fa)+(ft)-(F)$) -- (ft);
\pic[draw, "$20^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=F--A--T};
\pic[draw, "$15^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=T--B--F};
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[above left] at (F) {$F$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
An observer at $P$ due south of a vertical tower of height $h$ measures the angle of elevation to the top as $\alpha = 25^{\circ}$.
A second observer at $Q$ due east of the tower foot $F$ measures the angle of elevation as $\beta = 18^{\circ}$.
If the distance between the two observers is $PQ = 60\text{ m}$, calculate $h$ to the nearest metre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (F) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (-0.9,-1.7);
\coordinate (Q) at (2.7,-0.6);
\coordinate (T) at (0,2.5);
\draw[thick] (F) -- (T) node[midway, left] {$h$};
\draw[dashed] (F) -- (P);
\draw[dashed] (F) -- (Q);
\draw (P) -- (Q) node[midway, below right] {$60\text{ m}$};
\draw (P) -- (T);
\draw (Q) -- (T);
\coordinate (fp) at ($(F)!0.32cm!(P)$);
\coordinate (fq) at ($(F)!0.32cm!(Q)$);
\draw (fp) -- ($(fp)+(fq)-(F)$) -- (fq);
\coordinate (ft) at ($(F)!0.32cm!(T)$);
\draw (fp) -- ($(fp)+(ft)-(F)$) -- (ft);
\pic[draw, "$25^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=F--P--T};
\pic[draw, "$18^{\circ}$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=T--Q--F};
\node[below left] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\node[above left] at (F) {$F$};
\node[above] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

